      "extract": "Let $\\nu$ be a Borel measure on $\\mathbb{R}^{n}$. We say that $\\nu$ satisfies a Brunn--Minkowski inequality with exponent $a$ if for all Borel sets $K_{0}, K_{1} \\subseteq\\mathbb{R}^{n}$ satisfying $\\nu(K_{0}),\\nu(K_{1})>0$ and every $0\\le t \\le1$ we have $$\\label{eq:BM} \\nu\\left((1-t)K_{0}+ t K_{1}\\right)\\ge\\left((1-t)\\nu(K_{0})^{a}+ t \\nu(K_{1})^{a}\\right)^{1/a}.$$ Here $(1-t)K_{0} +t K_{1}=\\left\\{ (1-t) x+ t y:\\",
